<p>
  <.link navigate="/settings/documents">Settings → Documents &amp; branding</.link>
  sets how everything you print or send looks: quotes, sales orders, invoices, delivery notes,
  requests for quotation, purchase orders (LPOs), goods received notes (GRNs), stock notes and job
  cards. The preview on the right updates as you go; nothing changes until you click <strong>Save design</strong>.
</p>

<h2>Your logo</h2>
<p>
  Click <strong>Choose PNG, JPG or WebP</strong>, pick the file (up to 1 MB) and click <strong>Upload</strong>. A wide logo on a transparent background looks best. With several
  legal entities, pick the entity at the top: each has its own logo and design.
</p>

<h2>Style</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Classic</strong>: your name on the left, the document title on the right.</li>
  <li><strong>Modern</strong>: a band in your accent colour across the top.</li>
  <li><strong>Compact</strong>: smaller text and spacing, for long documents.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Accent colour</strong>
    colours the title, the line under the column headings and the total.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Font</strong>
    and <strong>logo size</strong>, and whether to print tax IDs and signature lines.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Wording per document</h2>
<p>
  Pick a document type and set its <strong>title</strong>
  (e.g. <em>Tax invoice</em>
  or <em>LPO</em>), <strong>terms</strong>
  printed under the lines, and a <strong>footer</strong>
  such as bank or M-Pesa details. Leave a field empty to use the default.
</p>
<.callout>
  Only owners, admins and people whose role includes
  <em>Upload the logo and design printed documents</em>
  can change the design.
</.callout>
